From 6db70ad68c5aa905977a8c6b5c1fea3e733e4106 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:03:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native postcard, seahash and script-compression
 codecs

Add the byte-level codecs the native Chronik needs to read and write the
Rust Chronik's database unchanged:

- postcard Writer/Reader: LEB128 varints, zigzag signed ints, raw u8/bool
  and fixed arrays, length-prefixed sequences/strings, Option tags, enum
  variant indices and maps, with the error texts of postcard 1.1.3 and
  the "Inconsistent DB: ..." messages chronik-db raises on bad values;
- seahash, a bit-exact port of the seahash crate's hash() (default keys),
  used for the lookup_tx_by_hash and lookup_blk_by_hash keys;
- script compression (Core's ScriptCompression), used for script group
  member keys and the scripthash index;
- hex and big/little-endian helpers.

The golden vectors come from the Rust code itself: a test-only exporter,
chronik/chronik-db/tests/export_native_golden.rs, encodes edge values and
every value struct chronik-db stores (SerBlock, BlockStats, SerTx,
SpentByEntry, TokenMeta, GenesisInfo, DbTokenTx, lookup lists) and writes
them to chronik/native/test/fixtures/codec.json, which is committed. The
native codec tests re-encode every case and require byte equality, so a
codec mismatch is caught before any writer can corrupt a shared database.

Tier: eCash
